# SIS Permanent Engineering Constitution (Index)

**Version:** 2.0 · **Status:** PERMANENT / MANDATORY  
**Full text:** `.cursor/architecture/SIS-CONSTITUTION.md`  
**Governance map:** `.cursor/architecture/GOVERNANCE-MAP.md`

Compliance is **automatic** on every task. The user must NOT repeat architecture/security/UI/platform rules.

## Priority Order (never invert)

```text
Security → Data integrity → Tenant isolation → Authorization → Architecture
→ Business/domain → API contracts → Constitution → Module boundaries
→ UI consistency → Platform adaptation → Responsive → Accessibility
→ Testability → Maintainability → Performance → Developer convenience
```

## Mandatory Workflow

```text
UNDERSTAND → INSPECT → IMPACT ANALYSIS → PLAN → IMPLEMENT → TEST → VALIDATE → REPORT
```

Before coding, read applicable:

```text
.cursor/rules/          .cursor/architecture/       .cursor/skills/
01-ARCHITECTURE.mdc     ARCHITECTURE-STACK.md       application-feature
sis-core.mdc            SIS-CONSTITUTION.md         database-change
clean-architecture.mdc  UI/WINDOW/RUNTIME/PLATFORM contracts
security.mdc            api-conventions.md
react-inertia.mdc       GOVERNANCE-MAP.md
10-MODULES.mdc          MODULE-CONTRACT.md
12-DOCUMENTATION.mdc
```

## Non-Negotiables

- **One business model** — no parallel logic in UI, React, controllers, or platform adapters
- **Server-side authorization** — hiding UI is not security
- **Backend validation is authoritative** — frontend validation is UX only
- **No hard-delete** of official academic records — status + `effective_to`
- **Tenant isolation** — school context + policy + RLS where enabled
- **Thin controllers** — handlers own transactions; Domain stays pure
- **Framework independence at contract level** — UI adapters consume API + auth + design tokens
- **No platform-specific business logic** (`if iPhone`, `if React`, etc.)

## STOP Conditions (request approval)

Destructive DB changes · security/authorization bypass · breaking API without migration · data loss · tenant isolation risk · new framework/runtime without impact analysis · requirements contradict mandatory rules.

## Definition of Done

Requirement + architecture + security + authorization + API + DB (if any) + responsive/adaptive considered + accessibility considered + tests + validation + no unexplained regression.

